This is the reason for abandoning this.

Since v1.6.3.260807_Alpha_Dev_1.4.3 (Build 27) completed practical testing on the ECHO server (tag),
we (the Archiv Security Monitoring System development team) planned to adjust the processing logic of
SuspiciousLoginAttemptsHandler::ProcessEventXml in v1.6.7.260808_Alpha_Dev_1.5.0 (Build 30) and later versions.

However, the main developer Byakuya (aka BiliBiliBaiye, DrifterByakuya, who is also a lead developer for Archiv and Aurarts Studios) pointed out:
although refactoring void SuspiciousLoginAttemptsHandler::ProcessEventXml(EVT_HANDLE hEvent) is a good idea,
introducing multi-IP address logging would cause a huge amount of work:

- We would have to split the string objects and get regional information one by one;
- All HTML files used for sending emails in the smtp/templates directory would need to be refactored.

Considering his current preparation for the college entrance exams, completing this work is unrealistic.
The internal Archiv Security team unanimously agreed with his view, so we decided to abandon this directory.
(After all, he has exams to focus on =￣ω￣=)

Of course, since the project is already open source,
we also welcome developers in the community to step in and help improve this feature.

Let’s wish Byakuya great success in the 2027 college entrance exams!
Also, may the students of Archiv and its partner teams achieve top scores in 2027 and in future exams!